## Why This Is Asked
Designed to test practical skills in modular design, dynamic config-driven provisioning, and CI governance for multi-environment Terraform.

## Key Concepts
- wrapper module tag injection
- dynamic resources via for_each and config.json
- per-env backend keys
- CI gate enforcing prod constraints

## Code Example
```terraform
# wrapper module interface
variable "environment" { type = string }
variable "cost_center" { type = string }
output "injected_tags" {
  value = merge({ Environment = var.environment }, { CostCenter = var.cost_center })
}
```

```json
// config.json
{
  "dev": { "buckets": ["dev-app-data"] },
  "prod": { "buckets": ["prod-app-data"] }
}
```

```hcl
# backend config sketch
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "tf-state"
    key    = "env/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate config.json before plan?
- How would you extend to include new environments without touching code?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests how a junior engineer models read-only environments, data sourcing, and per-env state management without touching prod resources. It mirrors real-world patterns at scale at top tech companies.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform data sources for read-only references
- Per-env backends to segregate state
- Avoiding resource creation in isolated environments

## Code Example
```javascript
data "aws_vpc" "inventory" {
  filter {
    name   = "tag:Environment"
    values = ["inventory"]
  }
}
data "aws_subnet" "inventory" {
  filter {
    name   = "vpc-id"
    values = [data.aws_vpc.inventory.id]
  }
}
```

```javascript
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "tf-state"
    key    = "inventory/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

```javascript
output "inventory_vpc_id" { value = data.aws_vpc.inventory.id }
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify that inventory plans never propose changes to prod data? 
- How would you automate inclusion of inventory in CI without accidentally applying prod changes?
